  "prefLabel": "Auc 501.01 Obligation To Obey",
  "priorExpiration": "2006-01-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Auc 501.01 Obligation To Obey. The ethical standards set forth in this part shall bind all licensees, and violation of any such standard shall be a basis for imposing disciplinary sanctions. Conduct proscribed by these ethical standards, when performed by an unlicensed person or during a prior period of licensure, shall also be a basis for denying a license application.\n\nSource. #6658, eff 1-1-98, EXPIRED: 1-1-06\n\nNew. #12201-B, eff 6-7-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/auc100-500.html"
}
